# Links the nightly sweep must not report. Every entry is a link that works
# for a reader and fails only for a checker running from a GitHub runner --
# an access policy, not link rot. AD-10 keeps third-party behaviour out of
# the report; these are the same principle at URL granularity.
#
# Each line needs a reason and, where it matters, what it costs us to skip.

# Cloudflare serves 403 to datacenter IPs. Confirmed 403 from both a GitHub
# runner and a local machine; the page is fine in a browser.
https://chatgpt\.com/

# Resets the connection from GitHub runners (os error 104) while answering
# 200 elsewhere. Cost of skipping: if the status page itself ever dies, this
# sweep stays quiet about it. Checked by hand when the FAQ is reverified.
https://status\.signalsapi\.com/
